---
Title: Images
---

# Images

An inline @image(figs/icon.png)[a small icon]{width=1em} sits inside its paragraph,
while the block form is a top-level element of its own.

@image+(figs/network.png)[A small-world graph]{width=0.6 align=center}

Dimensions may be a fraction of the text width, a quoted percentage, a bare unit,
a pair of units, or pixels — each translated for the format being written.

@image+(figs/a.png)[Percentage]{width="60%"}

@image+(figs/b.png)[Bare units]{width=8cm height=5cm}

@image+(figs/c.png)[Pixels]{width=400px}

@image+(figs/d.png)[Scaled]{scale=1.5}

A `tex-` or `web-` prefix confines a key to one output and beats the unprefixed
key there; anything untranslated passes through to the HTML as written.

@image+(figs/e.png)[Scoped]{width=0.5 tex-width=0.8 web-loading=lazy tex-options="trim=0 0 0 1cm, clip" class=plate id=fig-e}

@image+(figs/f.png)[Right-aligned]{width=0.3 align=right}

@image+(figs/g.png){width=0.3}

@image+(https://example.com/remote.png)[Remote]{width=0.4}

@image+(figs/vector.svg)[Vector art]{width=0.4}
